# type, prompt, options, correct indices or accepted text, explanation
B=[]
def add(t,q,o,a,e): B.append(dict(t=t,q=q,o=o.split('|') if o else [],a=a,e=e))
def m(q,o,a,e): add('M',q,o,[a],e)
def t(q,a,e): add('T',q,'True|False',[0 if a else 1],e)
def c(q,o,a,e): add('C',q,o,a,e)
def s(q,a,e): add('S',q,'',a.split('|'),e)
m('Yesterday, Kevin ___ a notebook.','buy|bought|buys|buying',1,'Bought is the past form of buy.')
m('Which verb is a regular verb?','Went|Took|Played|Saw',2,'Play becomes played.')
m('Which part of a recount introduces the people, time and place?','Events|Re-orientation|Conclusion|Orientation',3,'Orientation introduces the background.')
m('The students ___ tired after the competition.','were|was|is|be',0,'Use were with a plural subject in the past.')
m('Which expression asks for an opinion?','I totally agree.|Please come to my party.|What is your view on this?|I think it is useful.',2,'It asks what someone thinks.')
m('Which expression shows strong agreement?','Perhaps you are right.|Absolutely!|I am not sure.|I disagree.',1,'Absolutely shows strong agreement.')
m('I believe this activity ___ students learn better.','helping|help|helped yesterday|helps',3,'Activity is singular.')
m('Which information tells guests where an event will happen?','Venue|Date|Greeting|Signature',0,'Venue means the event location.')
m('Which language does RSVP originally come from?','Spanish|English|French|Italian',2,'RSVP comes from French.')
m('Which expression politely declines an invitation?','Count me in!|Thank you, but I have another plan.|Sure, I will come.|I would be happy to join.',1,'The speaker politely refuses.')
t('A recount text usually describes past experiences.',True,'A recount retells past experiences.')
t("She didn't visited the museum is grammatically correct.",False,"Use visit after didn't.")
t('In my view introduces a personal opinion.',True,'It introduces what someone thinks.')
t('RSVP means every invited guest must attend.',False,'RSVP asks guests to respond.')
t('An invitation can be delivered through a spoken conversation.',True,'Invitations can be spoken or written.')
c('Select all irregular past verbs.','Opened|Drank|Found|Cleaned',[1,2],'Drink and find are irregular verbs.')
c('Select all expressions used to give an opinion.','I believe this is helpful.|Would you like to join?|In my view, it is interesting.|I feel this is a good idea.',[0,2,3],'These introduce opinions.')
c('Which details tell guests when and where to attend?','Date|Time|Venue|Sender’s favorite color',[0,1,2],'Date, time and venue are event details.')
s('What is the term for rewriting an idea using different words without changing its meaning?','paraphrasing|paraphrase|to paraphrase','Paraphrasing keeps the original meaning.')
s('What does RSVP mean in English?','please respond|please reply|please answer|respond please|reply please','RSVP means please respond.')
p='Last Wednesday, Alina joined a cooking class. First, she prepared the ingredients. Next, she mixed the flour and eggs. Finally, she baked a cake. She was proud of her work.\n\n'
m(p+'What did Alina do immediately before baking?','Joined the class|Mixed the flour and eggs|Ate the cake|Bought the ingredients',1,'She mixed the ingredients before baking.')
m(p+'Which sentence is the re-orientation?','She was proud of her work.|She prepared the ingredients.|She mixed the flour and eggs.|Alina joined a cooking class.',0,'The final sentence expresses her feelings.')
m('Choose the best paraphrase of “The journey was exhausting.”','The journey was short.|The journey was exciting.|The journey made us very tired.|The journey never happened.',2,'Exhausting means making someone very tired.')
m('Liam: I think our classroom needs more plants.\nSofia: You may be right, but we need to take care of them every day.\nWhat does Sofia express?','Strong agreement|An invitation|Complete disagreement|Mild agreement with a concern',3,'She partly agrees but expresses a concern.')
m('Which expression is most suitable when asking the principal for an opinion?','Hey, what do you think?|May I ask for your opinion on this plan?|Tell me what you think now.|You agree, right?',1,'This is a polite formal expression.')
m('Choose the best paraphrase of “I believe school uniforms are useful.”','I think school uniforms are helpful.|I dislike wearing uniforms.|Everyone must buy a uniform.|School uniforms are expensive.',0,'Both express the same positive opinion.')
p='ART WORKSHOP\nDear Grade 8 Students,\nJoin our painting workshop on Friday at 2 p.m. in the art room. Bring your own paintbrush. Please confirm your attendance with Ms. Clara by Thursday.\nBest regards,\nArt Club\n\n'
m(p+'Who should students contact?','Their parents|The principal|Ms. Clara|The art room manager',2,'The invitation names Ms. Clara.')
m(p+'What is the function of Best regards?','Event title|Receiver’s name|Event details|Complimentary closing',3,'It is a polite closing expression.')
t('The words first, next and finally help readers understand the order of events.',True,'These time connectives organize events.')
t('A good paraphrase must change the original meaning.',False,'A paraphrase changes words, not meaning.')
t('Please confirm your attendance has a similar purpose to RSVP.',True,'Both ask guests to respond.')
t('A birthday invitation to a close friend must always use formal language.',False,'Informal language is suitable for friends.')
c('On Sunday, Noah helped his uncle at a farm. He fed the chickens, collected eggs and watered the plants. Although he was tired, he enjoyed the experience.\nSelect all correct statements.','Noah visited the farm on Sunday.|Noah bought some chickens.|Noah collected eggs.|Noah enjoyed helping his uncle.',[0,2,3],'These details are supported by the text.')
c('Which sentences use the simple past tense correctly?',"She didn't went home.|We watched a documentary.|Did he bring his camera?|They were nervous.",[1,2,3],"Use the base verb after didn't.")
c('Which opinions are supported by clear reasons?','I like the library because it is quiet.|I think the game is good.|I prefer walking because it keeps me healthy.|I believe recycling is useful because it reduces waste.',[0,2,3],'These opinions include reasons.')
c('Select the correct paraphrases of “Reading regularly helps us learn new words.”','Reading often improves our vocabulary.|Reading every day makes us forget words.|We can learn more words by reading often.|Learning words does not require reading.',[0,2],'Both keep the original meaning.')
c('Hey, Mia!\nCome to my board game afternoon this Saturday at 3 p.m. at my house. Let me know by Friday if you can come.\nSee you!\nElla\nWhich statements are correct?','It is a formal invitation.|Ella is the sender.|Mia should respond by Friday.|The event starts at 3 p.m.',[1,2,3],'The invitation is informal.')
s('We ___ (leave) the station at six yesterday.','left','Left is the past form of leave.')
s('Please reply by Friday to confirm whether you can attend. What is the common four-letter abbreviation for this instruction?','rsvp|r.s.v.p.','RSVP asks guests to respond.')
s('Complete the paraphrase using one word: I believe the task is simple. → I think the task is ___.','easy|simple|straightforward|uncomplicated','Easy has a similar meaning to simple.')
m('Last month, our class visited a science center. I expected the visit to be boring, but I changed my mind after trying the experiments. My favorite activity was building a small electric circuit. When we returned to school, I realized that science could be fun.\nHow did the writer’s opinion change?','From excited to disappointed|From uninterested to interested|From happy to angry|From confident to afraid',1,'The writer expected boredom but found science enjoyable.')
m('Choose the best paraphrase of “Although we arrived late, we managed to watch the performance.”','We missed the performance because we were late.|We arrived early to watch the performance.|Despite arriving late, we were able to watch the performance.|The performance started late because of us.',2,'The original meaning and contrast remain the same.')
m('Dylan: I think students should have less homework.\nAmelia: I understand your point, but some homework helps us remember the lessons.\nWhich statement describes Amelia’s response?','She completely supports Dylan.|She refuses to share an opinion.|She asks Dylan to do her homework.|She politely expresses a different view and gives a reason.',3,'Amelia disagrees politely and gives a reason.')
m('Which sentence best paraphrases “Group discussions allow students to learn from one another”?','Students can share knowledge and learn together through discussions.|Students should study alone during discussions.|Group discussions prevent students from learning.|Students must always agree with each other.',0,'Both explain learning from others.')
m('GREENFIELD JUNIOR HIGH SCHOOL\nSubject: Student Project Exhibition\nDear Parents,\nWe would be delighted to welcome you to our exhibition on 18 December at 9 a.m. in the school hall. Kindly reply to the school office by 15 December.\nRespectfully,\nMrs. Anita, Principal\nWhy are parents asked to reply by 15 December?','To change the exhibition date|To confirm attendance so the school can prepare|To submit their children’s projects|To become exhibition judges',1,'An RSVP helps the organizer prepare.')
m('Which sentence best paraphrases “Kindly inform us whether you will be able to attend”?','You must attend our event.|Tell us why you dislike the event.|Please let us know if you can come.|Please invite more people.',2,'Both ask guests to confirm attendance.')
t('Changing “I visited the zoo” to “I will visit the zoo” is a correct paraphrase of the same past experience.',False,'The second sentence changes the time to the future.')
t('Two people can express different opinions while still respecting each other.',True,'Disagreement can be polite.')
t('RSVP originally comes from the English language.',False,'RSVP originally comes from French.')
c('During the school sports festival, I joined a running competition. At first, I felt nervous because the other runners looked fast. When the race began, I tried my best. I finished third and felt proud because I had not given up.\nWhich conclusions are supported?','The writer won first place.|The writer was nervous before the race.|The writer felt proud despite not winning.|The writer continued trying until the end.',[1,2,3],'The writer finished third and was proud of the effort.')
c('Select all correct paraphrases of “The unexpected delay made us miss the beginning of the show.”','We missed the start of the show because of an unexpected delay.|The show was canceled before we arrived.|An unplanned delay caused us to miss the opening of the show.|We watched the entire show without any delay.',[0,2],'Both keep the original cause and result.')
c('Which features are commonly found in a recount text?','Past tense verbs|Time connectives|A list of commands as the main content|Events arranged in time order',[0,1,3],'Recounts retell past events in order.')
c('Eric: I believe school clubs help students discover their interests.\nLuna: I completely agree. They also help us make new friends.\nRyan: You may be right, but students need enough time to study.\nWhich statements are correct?','Luna expresses strong agreement.|Ryan completely agrees without any concern.|Eric gives an opinion.|Ryan expresses a concern about study time.',[0,2,3],'Ryan mentions a concern while partly agreeing.')
c('Which sentences are grammatically correct and give an opinion supported by a reason?','I think exercise are important because it keep us fit.|I believe music helps us relax because it reduces stress.|I think school trips are useful because students learn outside the classroom.|I believes books is helpful because they gives information.',[1,2],'Both use correct grammar and give reasons.')
c('RIVERDALE SCHOOL\nSubject: Charity Concert\nDear Parents,\nWe invite you to our charity concert on Saturday at 6 p.m. in the school auditorium. Please reply to the school secretary by Wednesday.\nYours sincerely,\nEvent Committee\nWhich statements are correct?','The parents are the receivers.|The event takes place in the auditorium.|The reply deadline is Saturday.|The Event Committee is the sender.',[0,1,3],'The reply deadline is Wednesday.')
c('Which statements about RSVP are correct?','RSVP originally comes from French.|RSVP requires every guest to attend.|RSVP helps the organizer prepare for the event.|RSVP asks guests to confirm whether they can attend.',[0,2,3],'RSVP requests a reply, not compulsory attendance.')
s('Correct the verb: Did your brother (took) the bus yesterday? Write only the correct verb.','take','Use the base verb after did.')
s('Complete the paraphrase: I share your opinion completely. → I completely ___ with you.','agree','Both express strong agreement.')
s('An invitation says: Venue: School auditorium. What is another English word for venue?','place|location|site','Venue means the place or location of an event.')
s('Subject: Annual Student Art Exhibition\nWhich part of the formal invitation is shown?','subject|subject line','The subject identifies the topic of the letter.')
assert len(B)==60
